+### `withoutQuery(input, keys?)`
+
+Removes the query section of a URL, or selected query keys, while preserving the raw bytes of the remaining URL and query fields.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2#frag"); // "/foo#frag"
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2", "bar"); // "/foo?baz=2"
+```
+Query keys are decoded using the same rules as `parseQuery`. When keys are
+supplied, retained fields are not decoded or re-serialized.
+
 ### `withoutTrailingSlash(input, respectQueryAndFragment?)`
 
 Removes the trailing slash from the URL or pathname.
